  "notes": "Clean lane: no new quantified exploit in chunk core. Known-ledger rows on internal/acdsl (security-MAJ-1-r2 lifetime=task exemption, security-MAJ-2-r1 rename detection, correctness-MAJ-9-r1 branch-chosen base_ref incl. moving the local base ref via update-ref, correctness-MAJ-10-r1 CRLF) not re-reported. Candidates examined and dropped: (1) ruleDelta/FileUniverse split git output on whitespace and see quoted non-ASCII paths, but both discovery and the delta drop such files alike, so no rule can hide in them; (2) verifier binaries under bin/verifiers and verifier source are outside policySurface, but tampering with them equals tampering with the bin/acdsl runner itself, outside any in-repo gate's threat model; (3) -registry flag path is relative to cwd while overlayViolations reads <root>/acdsl/registry.local.json - only reachable through the gate invoker's own flags, not a branch edit; (4) install.env value splices raw into settings JSON (ExpandInstallMarkers) - operator-owned file, no boundary; (5) sessions validateScopeName blocks traversal (.., /, \\, archived, Base mismatch incl. Windows volume forms). Removed scope: none - every manifest file read in full. Cross-chunk notes for the station: internal/server callers of Store.DeleteScope/ArchiveScope/UnarchiveScope (POST routes) should be checked for CSRF/origin protection since DeleteScope is an irreversible RemoveAll; evals EvalDir.Dir now carries a nested 'skill/date-hash' path with a slash - the server artifact route that resolves Dir+file must still confine to the evals root; repos namePattern still admits '.' and '..' as repo names (pre-existing) which reach sessions/<name> mining folders outside this chunk.",
